A||||6||Kage86GT4SP||Windshield scratch removal?||||1||
Z||000000||Kage86GT4SP||12-28-1999||07:49 PM||||While I was getting the frost off the windshield this a.m., I managed to cause several small scratches.  <P>Any ideas, techniques or products I can use to help with this?||||reg||1
Z||000001||mutfish||12-28-1999||08:58 PM||||The Eastwood co.(www.eastwoodco.com)sells a kit containing a polishing wheel and a jar of cerium oxide to remove windsheild scratches.If you can catch your fingernail in the scratch, it's probably is too deep to remove.....||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||12-28-1999||10:05 PM||||Just got a kit from JC Whitney containing the same w/polishing wheel for $28.00! My prob is with the drivers side door and I don't know if I should try to polish it cause I heard I could shatter it?||||reg||14
Z||000003||Monkeyman||12-28-1999||11:08 PM||||Only if you polish it with a hammer.  I've polished window glass on other cars before without any problems.  It wouldn't hurt to make sure the glass is as warm as possible.  (At least above freezing.)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Kage86GT4SP||12-29-1999||03:35 AM||||Thanks, guys.<P>The scratches ar very small width, but a concentrated at eye level.  Additionally, the windshield is all of about 4 months old, so it REALLY torqued me.  But I can get it done with your info... again, THANKS!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||dogtired||12-29-1999||03:36 AM||||I would recommend changing the scraper you are using??   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>Personally I think the scrapers with the metal strip in them should be outlawed.<BR>I know Ice is a pain in the GLass, but glass is expensieve.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>MonkeyMan probably used that BFH to clean his windows   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Be careful, I have also heard that your glass can shatter when trying to polish scratches.||||reg||6
Z||000006||Monkeyman||12-29-1999||11:35 AM||||I read the directions on the box.  It said something about a 3# sledge hammer, so I used one.  Turns out I was reading the wrong box.  Ooops!  Oh, well.  No one's perfect (although I am awfully close!  If I could just get rid of that pesky mental condition!)||||reg||1
